# Keep the working tree byte-identical to the repository.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout on Windows
# and not on Linux. CI asserts no CR bytes, so that gate would describe a
# Linux tree while saying nothing about the tree it was written on.
# Check what any given path will get with: git check-attr eol -- <path>
* text=auto eol=lf

# Recorded fixtures. json.dumps escapes control characters, so a CR byte
# in here is real content captured from a response body -- a page with a
# carriage return in its text -- not a line-ending artefact. Normalising
# it would corrupt the recording.
tests/fixtures/*.json -text

# Generated or binary content must never be line-ending normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.whl binary